    "nci_treatment": "Stream is the amount distributable to Unitholders only (excludes NCI S$11.2m equity and perpetual-securities distributions S$4.4m), so no NCI or perp deduction in the bridge.",
    "notes": "MODEL: REIT AFFO (distributable income) capitalisation at cost of equity, run through the component engine with net_debt = 0. Routed via dcf-methods SKILL.md row 'REIT / property trust (IAS 40 fair-value, external manager)'. MPACT is an externally managed (Mapletree) S-REIT; net income is dominated by fair-value moves (FY26 -S$114.8m IP revaluation, Q4 FY26 a net loss) so P/E and owner-FCF/WACC are meaningless. Engine mapping: revenue = gross revenue; 'ebitda_margin_path' = distributable income to Unitholders as % of gross revenue (FY26 48.6%); 'sbc_pct_path' = management fees paid in units % of revenue (2.07% FY26); 'capex_pct_path' = maintenance capex % of revenue (FY26 additions to investment properties S$86.6m include AEI; FY25 S$56.7m); D&A, cash tax and working capital zero because DI is already post-tax and post-working-capital. Distribution policy: at least 90% of taxable income; payout ~100% of DI in practice. FY26 DI includes S$27.3m capital distribution (FY25 S$49.9m) -- partly return-of-capital repatriation from overseas, treated as recurring in base, cut in bear. FY27 is the first full year without Mapletree Anson (divested Jul 2024), TSI/ASY (Aug 2025) and Festival Walk Tower office (Feb 2026); proceeds repaid debt (gearing 36.5%, ICR 3.2x at 31 Mar 2026). No Q1/H1 FY27 filing has been extracted; the last data point is FY26 (Mar 2026). Cross-check: NAV/unit S$1.73 at 31 Mar 2026; price/NAV ~0.68. Qualitative Analysis.json did not exist at build time; business context taken from the FY26 results announcement.",
